<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Prince Maximilian of Baden</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1867–1929</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Max von Baden, Prince Max of Baden</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Prince Maximilian of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baden">Baden</a> was a German liberal aristocrat who served as the last chancellor of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/german-empire">German Empire</a> in October and November 1918. He sought an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armistice-of-11-november-1918">armistice</a> with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allies">Allies</a> and on 9 November 1918 announced the abdication of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wilhelm-ii">Wilhelm II</a> on his own authority before handing power to the Social Democrat <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/friedrich-ebert">Friedrich Ebert</a>. In 1920 he founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/schule-schloss-salem">Schule Schloss Salem</a> with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kurt-hahn">Kurt Hahn</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/prince-maximilian-of-baden.jpg" alt="Prince Maximilian of Baden" width="320" height="444" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author Originally uploaded to Wikimedia Commons by BArchBot Cropped and reuploaded to Wikimedia... · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bundesarchiv_Bild_183-R04103,_Prinz_Max_von_Baden(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
